  "body": "## What changed\n\n`contour_disc_hole` and `contour_tangential_lead` were refused by the program gate. Their 3 mm leads on the R6 bore (6 mm tool, so the cutter centre runs on an r = 3 ring) lie on that ring's own circle, so the leads crossed it (`Warning::Crossing`). Yet both had posted NC goldens in every milling dialect, compared byte for byte by `conformance`.\n\nI took **option (a)** and moved the leads. Both fixtures now use **2 mm** leads (quarter arc and half arc). These sit inside the ring, tangent at the seam, and both programs verify clean. I probed 0.5 / 1 / 1.5 / 2 / 2.5 mm and all were clean; 2 mm leaves a full millimetre of margin. Each fixture still tests what it was made for:\n- `contour_disc_hole` still shows a tessellated round bore fitting to arcs. That comes from the ring, not the lead.\n- `contour_tangential_lead` still shows a half-arc lead posting as one `S±1` arc with a 2 x radius standoff (now 4 mm).\n\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/862-refused-program-goldens.md`.\n\n**The refusal is kept.** `solid_law_goldens::a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused` builds the old 3 mm programs on the same plate inside the test (no golden is kept for them). It asserts the exact crossing pairs the old verdicts carried: 6 for the arc lead, 12 for the tangential lead.\n\n**New guard.** `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes` walks every `.nc` under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/` whose stem is a `.cl` golden. Each one must meet one of three conditions:\n- a depth-law golden (judged by `verdicts()`) must verify clean;\n- a golden no depth law judges must be named in `UNJUDGED` with its reason (slots, trochoid, trace, `arc_planes`, `plasma_plate_with_holes`);\n- a golden of a refused program must carry `refused program, posted for syntax conformance` on its first line (option (c)'s door; nothing uses it today).\n\nSo a new posted golden is either judged or explicitly classified. Before the fix, the guard would fail on the 16 disc-hole `.nc` files.\n\n`every_depth_law_golden_verifies_exactly_as_before` now asserts that all 14 depth-law goldens verify clean.\n\n`solid_law_goldens.rs` was at 405 lines. Its plate/part builders (`rect`, `circle`, `region`, `walls`, `cap`, `plate`, `plate_cell`, `mill`) moved verbatim, now `pub`, into `crates/app/tests/common/solid_part.rs`. The two files are now 338 and 151 lines.\n\n## Goldens that moved (regenerated, none deleted)\n\nCL (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test golden_cl -- contour_disc_hole_matches_golden contour_tangential_lead_matches_golden`):\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/contour_disc_hole.cl`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/contour_tangential_lead.cl`\n\nNC (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance`), `contour_disc_hole.nc` and `contour_tangential_lead.nc` in each of:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/` (Fanuc)\n- `nc/haas/`, `nc/sinumerik/`, `nc/heidenhain/`, `nc/mazak/`, `nc/tormach/`, `nc/doosan-dnm/`, `nc/carvera/`\n\nThat is 18 files. No other golden moved, and no snapshot PNG was touched.\n\n**How they were checked.** I read the diffs; I did not just accept them.\n- Both CL files keep `moves=69`, and every move keeps its kind.\n- Only the lead-in/lead-out moves and the rapids/plunges to their start points moved; the ring and the outer contour are byte-identical.\n- I checked the new arcs by hand. The bore lead arc centre (19.951, 9.002) is 2.000 from its endpoints and 1.0 from the bore centre (= 3 - 2), so it is internally tangent to the ring.\n- The tangential lead's start point (20.049, 11.000) is 4.0 from the ring seam (19.853, 7.005), which is the 2r standoff.\n- The outer lead centre (40.576, -4.967) is 2.000 from (40.346, -2.98).\n- Every NC file keeps its line count (+/- balanced). The NC I/J words match the CL centres, e.g. Fanuc `G02 X40.346 Y-2.98 I-0.231 J1.986` and Heidenhain `I+40.576 J-4.967`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning:\n  - `solid_law_goldens::a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused` (the refusal)\n  - `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes` (the guard)\n  - `solid_law_goldens::every_depth_law_golden_verifies_exactly_as_before` (now all clean)\n- `#[test]` count: `solid_law_goldens` 1 -> 3; no other file changed its count. Before: 1, after: 3 (+2 new tests, none removed).\n- Gate, all on head `a78f977e`:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 278 camcraft-app test binaries, 2037 passed, 0 failed, 18 ignored. This includes `conformance`, `solid_law_goldens`, `golden_cl`, `posting`, `fanuc_post`, `heidenhain_block_form`, `arc_planes`, `tormach_post`, `tormach_end_units` and `program_comments`.\n  - The golden readers in other crates are green: `camcraft-post` `post_engine` (33/33) and `camcraft-cl` `headless_bin` (3/3; its `moves: 69 (... arcs 33)` stat holds).\n  - Each of the three pinning tests passes on its own via `cargo xtask gate test <name> --crate camcraft-app --binary solid_law_goldens --exact`.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `plasma_plate_with_holes` is named in `UNJUDGED`: its plasma program is not run through the plasma gate here. That is the same as before, just named now.\n- The slot, trace and trochoid goldens get no gate verdict in this suite. No depth law runs on them, as the suite header already said.\n- No GUI, and no release-lane heavy tests.\n\nChangelog: none (test fixtures and goldens only; no product code changes)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #862\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
